WEBVTT

00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:15,900
A blood work shows red blood cells are lower near anemia.

00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:21,500
Is the solution to take iron supplement or are there other ways to treat anemia that

00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,660
is with the rife machine?

00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:29,660
The good news is that two weeks on the nightly rife by white blood cell count went from 143

00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:36,620
to 118, or in the past it was rapidly trending upwards since this person has a blood cancer

00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:44,060
and they have elevated white blood cell count, so everybody here knows that your white blood cell

00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:52,700
count should be about 4 to 6.5, so this elevated white blood cell count is a blood cancer.

00:00:54,140 --> 00:01:00,620
So what do you do with red blood cells that are low?

00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:06,860
So you have an anemia, you have low red blood cells, probably elevated MCV, MCHC,

00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:13,900
RDW, so you have other signs of anemia plus low red blood cell count.

00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:17,980
Can you take iron for that?

00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:24,620
So it partly depends upon the cancer and it partly depends on how anemic a person is.

00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:29,420
If you're just near anemia but you're still within normal range,

00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:36,380
if somebody has a solid tumor cancer, I would say no, let's be careful not to give iron.

00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:40,380
By solid tumor cancer, I mean like breast cancer, liver cancer, colon cancer,

00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:50,860
not a leukemia or multiple myeloma. So the leukemia is multiple myeloma and even sub lymphomas,

00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:56,540
you could readily use iron. The reason why I say that is if you have a

00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:04,140
a solid tumor cancer like breast cancer, colon cancer, prostate cancer, etc.,

00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:12,460
giving iron to that, even in the case of a person having anemia, if you give iron, iron

00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:17,660
can actually feed the cancer. That doesn't typically take place, almost never takes place with

00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:22,780
the blood cancer, so the leukemia is an lymphoma. Typically you don't have to worry so much about that

00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:31,020
at all and you could treat the anemia with iron. But I would want to see your labs because just because

00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:37,420
you have low red blood cells, doesn't mean that it's necessarily iron deficiency anemia. It could

00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:42,460
be B12 anemia, it could be B6 anemia, it could be folate anemia. There's multiple different types

00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:54,380
of anemia in you. You discover that by looking at the other values. So the RDW, MCV, MCHC,

00:02:55,980 --> 00:03:04,380
and some other things you want to look at in the CBC. So that's what we'd want to look

00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:10,700
to really see, should we give this person iron? Because there's some rules in my book at least,

00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:15,500
you could have low red blood cells, oh, I have dear anemia, but your ferritid is super high,

00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:22,700
that you never give iron to somebody who's got high ferritid. So we'd want to look at the rest of

00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:29,340
the blood work before we'd say, oh, you have anemia, let's low red blood cells, dear anemia,

00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:35,660
let's just assume it's iron deficiency anemia and let's just assume that you're okay to take it because

00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:47,900
your ferritid is normal. We need to look at that in the more specific, but that's a great question.

